Template: mod-host/audio-device
Type: select
Choices: ${choices}
Description: USB audio device for mod-host:
 Select the USB audio device that should be used with JACK and mod-host.
 When this device is plugged in, the JACK audio server and mod-host will
 start automatically.
 .
 If your device is not listed, make sure it is plugged in and run
 'dpkg-reconfigure mod-host' to detect it.

Template: mod-host/audio-device-manual
Type: string
Default:
Description: Manual USB device specification (vendor:product:alsa_name):
 No USB audio devices with both playback and capture were detected.
 Enter the device specification manually as vendor_id:product_id:alsa_name.
 For example: 1397:0508:U192k
 .
 You can find the vendor and product IDs using 'lsusb', and the ALSA
 device name using 'cat /proc/asound/cards'.
